    "fixed": {
      "word": "FIXED",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Securely placed or fastened; settled; established; firm; imovable; unalterable.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Chem.)",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Stable; non-volatile. Fixed air (Old Chem.), carbonic acid or carbon dioxide; -- so called by Dr. Black because it can be absorbed or fixed by strong bases. See Carbonic acid, under Carbonic. potash, in distinction from the volatile alkali ammonia. together in a case ready for loading. mortars intended to remain stationary; -- distinguished from movable battery. a common menstruum, without great difficulty, as gold, platinum, lime, etc. one which emits constant beams; -- distinguished from a flashing, revolving, or intermittent light. and olein, which leave a permanent greasy stain, and which can not be distilled unchanged; -- distinguished from volatile or essential oils. troops wheels. same apparent position and distance with respect to each other, thus distinguished from planets and comets.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        }
      ],
